# Mole clean whitelist (mo clean / mo optimize).
#
# IMPORTANT: this file REPLACES mole's built-in defaults rather than adding to
# them (bin/clean.sh: the DEFAULT_WHITELIST_PATTERNS branch only runs when this
# file is absent). The upstream defaults are reproduced below verbatim -- when
# bumping mole, re-check lib/core/base.sh:DEFAULT_WHITELIST_PATTERNS for new
# entries. Only $FINDER_METADATA_SENTINEL is re-merged automatically.
#
# Matching: entries without a glob also protect everything beneath them, so a
# bare volume root covers the whole drive.
#
# Only `mo clean` and `mo optimize` consult this file. `mo purge` and the
# delete key in `mo analyze` do NOT -- they can still touch these paths.

# --- External data drives (greg-zone vaults, backups) ---
# mo clean only reaches a volume via `mo clean --external <path>`, where it
# would remove <volume>/.Trashes and <volume>/.TemporaryItems. These entries
# make that a no-op on the drives holding real data.
/Volumes/T7
/Volumes/T7-B
/Volumes/Lacie
/Volumes/LaCie
/Volumes/Wokyis M.2 SSD - Storage
/Volumes/Wokyis M.2 SSD - Time Machine

# --- This repo ---
# mo clean's project-artifact scan walks $HOME/*/ and removes __pycache__,
# .next/cache and .dart_tool. Some .pyc files under the Alfred workflows in
# mac-productivity/ are tracked, so an unprotected clean dirties the repo and
# breaks the stowed workflow until `git checkout`.
$HOME/greg_projects/dotfiles

# --- Upstream defaults (mole 1.50.0, lib/core/base.sh) ---
$HOME/Library/Caches/ms-playwright*
$HOME/.cache/huggingface*
$HOME/.m2/repository/*
$HOME/.gradle/caches/*
$HOME/.gradle/daemon/*
$HOME/.ollama/models/*
$HOME/Library/Caches/com.nssurge.surge-mac/*
$HOME/Library/Application Support/com.nssurge.surge-mac/*
$HOME/Library/Caches/org.R-project.R/R/renv/*
$HOME/Library/Caches/pypoetry/virtualenvs*
$HOME/Library/Caches/JetBrains*
$HOME/Library/Caches/com.jetbrains.toolbox*
$HOME/Library/Caches/tealdeer/tldr-pages
$HOME/Library/Application Support/JetBrains*
$HOME/Library/Caches/com.apple.finder
$HOME/Library/Mobile Documents*
